sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5170796-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5170796</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5497779-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5497779</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5772601-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5772601</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1997012542-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1997012542</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1177762A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAN JIE</name><address><country>CN</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAN, JIE</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAN JIE</name><address><country>CN</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAN, JIE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method and apparatus for continuous and noninvasive blood pressure measurement. The included angle and torsion angle between dorsal surface of hand and for arm at the wrist are respectively fixed on value that is adaptable for measuring blood pressure of radial arterial, placing a pressure ballonet and an array of arterial pulse wave sensor on the skin surface of radial arterial under wrist. By the theory of volume oscillating method and volume compensation method, the blood pressure of radial arterial or/and ulnar arterial can be measured continuously or discontinuously.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne procédé et dispositif de mesure en continu et non invasive de la tension artérielle qui consiste à fixer respectivement l'angle du dos de la main opposé à la partie intérieure du poignet et l'articulation de l'avant bras au niveau du poignet pour mesurer de la manière la plus convenable la tension artérielle d'une artère radiale, à placer un ballonnet de pression et un réseau de capteurs du pouls artériel sur la surface de la peau de l'artère radiale sous le poignet. Grâce aux principes de l'oscillométrie et de la compensation en termes du diamètre des vaisseaux sanguins, on peut mesurer en continu ou par intermittence la tension artérielle de l'artère radiale et/ou l'artère cubitale.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>